CellStructureMech license scope
===============================

Project-authored data, including curated records, annotations, mappings and
data exports, are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC-BY-4.0). See LICENSE-DATA.

Project-authored code, including software, scripts, tests, schemas and website
templates, is licensed under BSD-3-Clause. See LICENSE-CODE.

Project-authored narrative documentation is licensed under CC-BY-4.0. For
attribution, identify CellStructureMech and its contributors, link to
https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CellStructureMech, retain applicable source
attributions and indicate changes.

Third-party data, images, text, vendored code and other redistributed material
retain their own licenses and notices. The project licenses apply only to
material for which the project has licensing rights; they do not replace
upstream terms.

Previously released material remains available under the licenses offered
with those releases.

Third-party material and hosting policy
--------------------------------------

  * Hosted images under data/images/ and pages/img/. Each carries its own
    licence, the attribution its licence requires, its source accession and
    URL, in the `images` block of the record that displays it. Only CC0,
    public-domain, and CC BY material is hosted; see below.

  * Text and identifiers derived from CC BY sources — notably the UniProt
    Subcellular Location vocabulary (CC BY 4.0) and Complex Portal (CC BY 4.0).
    Every such claim names its source in an evidence reference or an xref.

Which licences may be hosted:

  * CC0 and public domain — no condition to carry.
  * CC BY — hosted with the attribution its licence requires, recorded per
    item and rendered on the record page.
  * CC BY-SA — NOT hosted. Share-alike constrains the licence of derivative
    works rather than merely requiring credit, so hosting it inside this CC BY
    corpus would conflict with the project's hosting policy. Cite and link
    instead.
  * CC BY-NC, CC BY-ND, and anything unverified — NOT hosted. Cite and link.

This split is machine-checked: the schema's licence enum, a corpus test, and
scripts/check_source_queue.py all refuse to host a licence not listed above.
